    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d660">

                <pb facs="0777" n="703" xml:id="pg703"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2895</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-07T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 7, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.55 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2876. Referring to my 2833 of September 27, 10 a.m.,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d660-f1"/> and 2830, September 26, 2 p.m.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d660-f2"/> The Danish Minister for Foreign Affairs informs me that
                    his Government is inclined to adopt the view of their Minister at Petrograd who
                    suggests in view of the strong collective protest made by the neutral
                    representatives at the capitol under date of the 5th September<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d660-f3"/> with which the German Consul General associated himself
                    against the imprisonment <hi rendition="#italic">en masse</hi> of persons of all
                    ages and both sexes and the daily summary executions indulged in by the soldiers
                    of the Red Army and the fact that the reign of terror is steadily subsiding,
                    that the Danish Government should take no further action of that character for
                    the moment. He suggests, however, that the Allied Governments and the United
                    States might associate themselves with the <hi rendition="#italic">démarche</hi>
                    of the 5th ultimo, the text of which I am sending by pouch together with
                    Chicherin’s reply, and the protest of the Diplomatic Corps against the violation
                    of the British Embassy building with its attendant outrages.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d660-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>Copy to London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
